The issue appears to be in the **focus event listeners** that are automatically expanding sections when users tab through the form. The problem is on these lines:

**Line 2499-2505** (H section):
```javascript
harmSectionHeader.addEventListener('focus', function(e) {
    // Auto-expand when focused via keyboard
    const checkboxes = document.getElementById('thriveHCheckboxes');
    if (checkboxes.classList.contains('collapsed')) {
        toggleHarmSection();
    }
});
```

**Line 2516-2522** (E section):
```javascript
engagementSectionHeader.addEventListener('focus', function(e) {
    // Auto-expand when focused via keyboard
    const checkboxes = document.getElementById('thriveEngagementCheckboxes');
    if (checkboxes.classList.contains('collapsed')) {
        toggleEngagementSection();
    }
});
```

The sections are automatically expanding when they receive focus (like when tabbing through the form), and then the blur listeners are collapsing them again, causing rapid opening/closing.

To fix this, you should remove the auto-expand on focus behavior. The sections should only toggle when explicitly activated with Enter or Space keys, not just by receiving focus.

